WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
The first film followed a receptor as it loaded a G protein.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.440
If an empty receptor already signals, where can a ligand move the response?

3
00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:23.127
A receptor population can signal even when every binding pocket is empty.

4
00:00:24.447 --> 00:00:28.227
Individual receptors sample less-active and more-active shapes.

5
00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:34.907
If some active shapes engage G proteins, the population produces basal activity.

6
00:00:36.187 --> 00:00:40.787
That starting signal becomes the reference for classifying what a ligand does.

7
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.800
An agonist raises signaling above that line.

8
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.240
In the simple picture, it favors the more-active receptor population.

9
00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.960
Gold agonist blocks settle into open receptor pockets.

10
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:60.000
More receptors remain signaling-competent, so the meter rises.

11
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.540
Agonist describes the measured effect, not merely the ability to bind.

12
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.290
A neutral antagonist behaves differently.

13
00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.330
By itself, it leaves basal signaling approximately unchanged.

14
00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.010
Its job appears when another ligand arrives.

15
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:24.430
Antagonist blocks occupy the pockets, so the incoming agonist finds few free

16
00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:30.370
receptors. At this agonist dose, the meter stays near basal instead of rising.

17
00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:34.850
Neutral describes the drug's effect on basal activity.

18
00:01:35.983 --> 00:01:39.323
An inverse agonist moves the response below basal.

19
00:01:40.643 --> 00:01:44.883
In the simple picture, it favors the less-active receptor population.

20
00:01:46.363 --> 00:01:49.123
Red-edged ligand blocks settle into those receptors.

21
00:01:50.603 --> 00:01:53.863
Fewer receptors engage G proteins, and the meter falls.

22
00:01:55.223 --> 00:01:59.583
The prefix inverse refers to signaling direction, not to opposite binding.

23
00:02:00.733 --> 00:02:04.193
Now remove measurable basal activity from the assay.

24
00:02:05.513 --> 00:02:06.773
The meter starts at zero.

25
00:02:08.013 --> 00:02:10.453
A neutral antagonist cannot lower it.

26
00:02:11.593 --> 00:02:14.533
Neither can an inverse agonist reveal a further decrease.

27
00:02:15.753 --> 00:02:17.573
Added alone, they look the same.

28
00:02:18.893 --> 00:02:23.693
Distinguishing them requires a receptor system with a visible basal signal.

29
00:02:24.783 --> 00:02:30.243
Real ligands can produce intermediate changes, even at a saturating concentration.

30
00:02:31.883 --> 00:02:37.503
Carazolol, bound in inactive β2-adrenergic receptor structures, is a partial inverse

31
00:02:37.503 --> 00:02:44.443
agonist. In an assay, it lowers basal signaling without producing the full reduction

32
00:02:44.443 --> 00:02:49.743
possible there. Efficacy means the response a bound ligand can produce.

33
00:02:49.743 --> 00:02:56.063
Partial describes its efficacy in that measured pathway, not incomplete binding in

34
00:02:56.063 --> 00:02:57.063
this assay.

35
00:02:57.717 --> 00:03:03.437
The active-versus-inactive picture is a useful first model, not a claim of only two

36
00:03:03.437 --> 00:03:07.897
rigid structures. Receptors sample ensembles of shapes.

37
00:03:09.257 --> 00:03:12.037
Efficacy is measured for one response in one cell.

38
00:03:13.277 --> 00:03:16.877
A ligand classed in one assay may class differently in another.

39
00:03:18.217 --> 00:03:22.357
Keep the meter and assay beside the receptor whenever you name efficacy.

40
00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.290
Use one reference line and three questions.

41
00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.110
Does the ligand raise signaling above basal?

42
00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:34.970
Does it leave basal unchanged while blocking another ligand?

43
00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.270
Or does it lower signaling below basal?

44
00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:45.870
Those observations separate agonism, neutral antagonism, and inverse agonism without

45
00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.510
pretending the receptor is a simple switch.
